/code-review high — loop U4-late1, round 1, range a8dff9b..df16e1c (engine is branch-scoped)

The review found 10 findings. None of them breaks the shipped sync logic, and all 16 test cases pass.

- **Most important:** the android setup task (finding 1) still tells consumers to edit the old folder `conf.d/_repo/`. It is already noted as gap G1, but no unit in the plan fixes it.
- **Next:** the new `zz-repo` guard checks only the names of the tool folders. A tool can still ship its own `conf.d/` folder that sorts after `zz-repo` and override the repository's settings (finding 2).
- **Docs:** findings 3 and 4 are about docs that no longer match the code. Finding 4's CLAUDE.md docs are planned for U5 (wave 3), so they are a problem only if the branch lands before U5.
- **The rest:** findings 5 and 6 are design choices, 7 and 8 are missing tests, and 9 and 10 are cleanups. I did not include an upgrade warning for consumers who still have `conf.d/_repo/`, because the plan and your standing rule leave upgrade paths out of scope.

